      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xspips__eeprom__polled__example_1gaf156542e10fb69ebb3a0760a22f77fbb" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int SpiPsEepromPolledExample</definition>
        <argsstring>(XSpiPs *SpiInstancePtr, UINTPTR BaseAddress)</argsstring>
        <name>SpiPsEepromPolledExample</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_spi_ps" kindref="compound">XSpiPs</ref> *</type>
          <declname>SpiInstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>UINTPTR</type>
          <declname>BaseAddress</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Illustrates how to use the <ref refid="struct_x_spi_ps" kindref="compound">XSpiPs</ref> device driver in polled mode. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This test writes and reads data from a serial EEPROM. The serial EEPROM part must be present in the hardware to use this example.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">SpiInstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the Spi Instance. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">BaseAddress</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The base address of the device.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if successful else XST_FAILURE.</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>- The function calls functions which contain loops that may be infinite if interrupts are not working such that it may not return. If the device slave select is not correct and the device is not responding on bus it reads a status of 0xFF for the status register as the bus is pulled up.<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>In XSCT/classic flow, the device configuration is looked up based on DeviceId. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
